       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave doesn't explain why the dose is 50 mg. A family visit and evening rounds don't make five times the maximum dose safe. A dose that size could cause dangerous hypotension and shock, and I'd be putting that risk on the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily. If the aim is to get blood pressure control started before evening rounds, I can enter it immediately.\n- **Help you escalate.** If you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, pharmacy or the attending should review it first. A clinical pharmacist can check the dose and suggest alternatives. These could include adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, which is usually safer than going above the maximum amlodipine dose.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
